From 21da50a63393d5cefb05e0ab22b69a0631dcbb70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:05:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] QVulkanWindow: give a window that asks for stereo buffers
 two views

QVulkanWindow built its swapchain with one image layer and gave its
renderer one framebuffer a frame, so a program asking for stereo buffers
(QSurfaceFormat::StereoBuffers) was shown flat even where the surface
offers two image layers ("imageArrayLayers must be greater than 0 and
less than or equal to the maxImageArrayLayers member of the
VkSurfaceCapabilitiesKHR structure",
VUID-VkSwapchainCreateInfoKHR-imageArrayLayers-01275).

It now asks for two views as Qt's own Vulkan swapchain does: the platform
answers with the window's "_q_stereo_views" native resource where it
knows more, the requested format decides elsewhere. Where the surface
offers them the swapchain has two image layers, each image a view and a
framebuffer per eye with the default render pass, a multisample color
image per eye and the depth-stencil buffer shared, and the platform hears
the views and the device it got. currentFramebuffer(), swapChainImageView(),
msaaColorImage() and msaaColorImageView() take a StereoTargetBuffer; with
one view they return the left eye's for both, so a renderer draws the
right eye when its framebuffer differs. The right eye's resources are
released by their own handles, whatever the next swapchain has.

A renderer that never asks for the right eye's framebuffer or image view
gets its left eye copied into the right one at the end of each frame, as
an OpenGL program drawing to GL_BACK on a stereo window fills both, so a
program that asked for stereo buffers without drawing an eye is shown
flat, not with an undefined right eye.

The Wayland Vulkan window's format says what its surface has once the
swapchain's maker said it, also when one view was given.

A test row, vulkanWindowTwoViews, checks the two framebuffers and image
views where the surface offers two layers (QTEST_STEREO_TWO_VIEWS=1 makes
a surface that does not a failure), the left eye's for both without the
request, and the grab's left eye.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
